From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darrel Griet <dgriet@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 21:16:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth: Request a longer LE supervision timeout on swift

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [swift/WCNSS hardware workaround]

The WCNSS controller intermittently stops servicing an encrypted LE
link for up to ~17s at a time and then recovers on its own -- this
happens in every configuration (central or peripheral, bluedroid or
BlueZ), so it is a controller firmware limitation. Stock WearOS with
Gadgetbridge rides through the identical stalls because bluedroid
negotiates a 20s link supervision timeout; at the BlueZ default of
5s (or an earlier 15s attempt, which the ~17s stalls still exceeded)
the link is torn down with HCI 0x08. Request a 30s supervision
timeout -- both in the peripheral-initiated connection parameter
update and when answering the central's remote connection parameter
request -- so the connection survives the stall as it does on stock.
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_event.c  |  6 ++++++
 net/bluetooth/l2cap_core.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
index ddbd9275bc28..bf379531b317 100755
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
@@ -5063,6 +5063,12 @@ static void hci_le_remote_conn_param_req_evt(struct hci_dev *hdev,
 			latency = 0;
 	}
 
+	/* Also lengthen the supervision timeout (see l2cap_le_conn_ready):
+	 * ride through the WCNSS RF-servicing stall instead of dropping. */
+	if (timeout < 0x09c4 &&
+	    !hci_check_conn_params(min, max, latency, 0x0bb8))
+		timeout = 0x0bb8;
+
 	if (hcon->role == HCI_ROLE_MASTER) {
 		struct hci_conn_params *params;
 		u8 store_hint;
diff --git a/net/bluetooth/l2cap_core.c b/net/bluetooth/l2cap_core.c
index eda4304b5dde..9cff561f19dd 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/l2cap_core.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/l2cap_core.c
@@ -1488,11 +1488,23 @@ static void l2cap_le_conn_ready(struct l2cap_conn *conn)
 	    (hcon->le_conn_interval < hcon->le_conn_min_interval ||
 	     hcon->le_conn_interval > hcon->le_conn_max_interval)) {
 		struct l2cap_conn_param_update_req req;
+		u16 to_multiplier = hcon->le_supv_timeout;
+
+		/*
+		 * WCNSS BLE workaround: the controller briefly (~7s) stops
+		 * servicing an encrypted LE link under load and then recovers;
+		 * at the default 5s supervision timeout the central drops the
+		 * link (HCI 0x08) before it heals. Ask the central for a
+		 * longer supervision timeout so the connection rides through
+		 * the stall instead of disconnecting.
+		 */
+		if (to_multiplier < 0x09c4)	/* 6.0 s */
+			to_multiplier = 0x0bb8;	/* 15.0 s */
 
 		req.min = cpu_to_le16(hcon->le_conn_min_interval);
 		req.max = cpu_to_le16(hcon->le_conn_max_interval);
 		req.latency = cpu_to_le16(hcon->le_conn_latency);
-		req.to_multiplier = cpu_to_le16(hcon->le_supv_timeout);
+		req.to_multiplier = cpu_to_le16(to_multiplier);
 
 		l2cap_send_cmd(conn, l2cap_get_ident(conn),
 			       L2CAP_CONN_PARAM_UPDATE_REQ, sizeof(req), &req);
-- 
